.TH DOVY 1 "" "dovy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dovy \- install software Debian stable lacks, from signed recipes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dovy
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B dovy
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dovy
installs software that Debian stable does not ship, newer versions of
software it does, and system setup such as backports, firmware and drivers.
.PP
Each piece of software is described by a recipe in a signed catalog.
.B dovy
builds a Debian package from the recipe on this machine, places it in a local
repository, and installs it with apt in one transaction. Every change is
shown as a plan and confirmed first. dpkg and apt remain the record of what
is installed.
.PP
.B dovy
runs as a regular user and asks for
.BR sudo (8)
when it needs root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI install " recipe" ...
Plan, confirm and install the recipes, with the recipes they depend on.
.TP
.BI remove " recipe" ...
Plan, confirm and remove the recipes. Debian packages a recipe replaced come
back. A recipe another installed recipe needs is refused.
.TP
.B update
Fetch the newest catalog release and verify its signature. Releases that are
not signed by a trusted key, or that need a newer
.BR dovy ,
are skipped with the reason. Nothing on the system changes.
.TP
.B upgrade
One plan for everything: the catalog, then
.B dovy
itself if a newer version is out, alone, after which the new version plans
the rest: recipes with new versions, and Debian's own upgrade.
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-installed " | " \-\-updates " | " \-\-orphaned ]
The recipes in the catalog, or only those installed, with an update, or no
longer in the catalog.
.TP
.BI search " word"
Recipes whose name or description contains the word.
.TP
.BI show " recipe" " \fR[\fP\-\-recipe \fR|\fP \-\-diff\fR]\fP"
Details of a recipe.
.B \-\-recipe
prints the recipe file;
.B \-\-diff
the changes since the installed version.
.TP
.B check
Report problems with the catalog, dovy's files and installed recipes.
Changes nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the commands. After a command, print its usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print dovy's version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failed, or
.B check
found problems.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong usage.
.TP
.B 3
Refused: a rule or a check stopped the plan; nothing changed.
.TP
.B 4
Cancelled: the plan was declined or interrupted; nothing changed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dovy/catalog
The catalog: a git clone of the newest trusted release
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/dovy/catalog ).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/dovy
Downloads, builds and the build sandbox
.RB ( $XDG_CACHE_HOME/dovy ).
.TP
.I /var/lib/dovy/repo
The local repository of packages dovy built.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dovy
dovy's records: the catalog release last used, the run in progress.
.TP
.I /var/log/dovy
One log per run.
.TP
.I /etc/dovy/keys.d
Extra trusted catalog keys for this machine, in git's allowed-signers
format. Files must be owned by root and writable by no one else.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/dovy.sources
apt's source for the local repository.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, output has no colour.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Where the catalog is kept; default
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where downloads and builds are kept; default
.IR ~/.cache .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR sudo (8)
.PP
https://github.com/getdovy/dovy
